*: Initiate a moderate AMZN position in tranches: buy roughly one-third to one-half of the intended exposure at current levels near $271.58, scale in the remainder on a pullback toward the 255\u2013260 zone, and place a disciplined stop below the breakout base near $226.65. Time horizon 3\u20136 months, reassessing if TTM FCF fails to improve or AWS growth decelerates materially from 37%.\n\n**Investment Thesis**: The operating engine is genuinely strong and accelerating: Q2 net sales grew 20% to $200.6B, AWS accelerated to +37% with operating income jumping to $27.5B from $19.2B [src-amzn] \u2014 recurring, not one-off. However, the bear and neutral analysts correctly flag earnings-quality concerns: the $62.6B net income is inflated by a $53.4B non-recurring Anthropic gain [src-amzn], and TTM FCF is a negative $7.6B outflow [src-amzn]. Technically, the stock is extended \u2014 ~11% above the Bollinger middle and ~12% above VWMA, RSI at 64.04, ATR of 9.26 [market-amzn] \u2014 so chasing the full 20% spike is risky. The neutral analyst's refinement is sound: trim the initial tranche to one-third rather than half at the most extended point, keep the 255\u2013260 scale-in, and respect that ATR of 9.26 (~3.4% daily swing) demands moderate sizing. This is a constructive Overweight, not a conviction Buy, given negative FCF and diluted earnings quality. Ticker AMZN, analysis date 2026-07-31, latest close $271.58 [market-amzn].\n\n**Price Target**: 300.0\n\n**Time Horizon**: 3-6 months\n",
